    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.244,
      0.037,
      0.293,
      0.475
    ],
    "text": "Law of good Gestalt. Elements of objects tend to be",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-10:text-3",
    "page_id": 10,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.298,
      0.036,
      0.488,
      0.493
    ],
    "text": "perceptually grouped together if they form a pattern that is regular, simple,and orderly.This law implies that as individuals perceive the world,they eliminate complexity and unfamiliarity so they can observe a reality in its most simplistic form. Eliminating extraneous stimuli helps the mind create meaning.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-10:text-4",
    "page_id": 10,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.523,
      0.037,
      0.671,
      0.49
    ],
    "text": "This meaning created by perception implies a global regularity, which is often mentally prioritized over spatial relations.The law of good gestalt focuses on the idea of conciseness,which is what all of gestalt theory is based on.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
